<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">FIFA World Cup</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as World Cup</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The FIFA World Cup is the international association football championship for men's national teams, organised every four years by FIFA since the first tournament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> in 1930, except in 1942 and 1946. It is the most widely watched sporting event in the world. Hosting it has become a source of national prestige, as for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 2010 and for Qatar in 2022, the first host in the Arab world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fifa-world-cup.jpg" alt="FIFA World Cup" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kitzbuehel_slalom_ganslernhang_2010.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
